# Windsurf Rules — azure-cosmos-db OCaml SDK

## Build & Compile
- Always use this command to compile and format: `dune build @fmt --auto-promote @ocaml-index`
- Always use this command to run tests: `dune runtest`

## Language & Toolchain
- OCaml with dune build system
- Three packages: `azure-cosmos-db` (core), `azure-cosmos-db-lwt`, `azure-cosmos-db-eio`
- ATD/atdgen for JSON types (`*.atd` → `*_t.ml`, `*_j.ml`)

---

## Module Structure

New shared logic belongs in `src/cosmos/` as its own `.ml`/`.mli` file pair. Backend-specific code goes in `src/cosmos_lwt/` or `src/cosmos_eio/`. Never duplicate logic between backends.

Every new public module must have a `.mli`. Keep `databases_intf.ml` as the canonical home for module type signatures (`IO`, `Http_client`, `Auth_key`).

**Types with operations belong in a module with `type t`, not at the top level.**

```ocaml
(* WRONG — type and functions scattered at top level *)
type indexing_directive = Include | Exclude
let string_of_indexing_directive = function Include -> "Include" | Exclude -> "Exclude"

(* RIGHT — grouped in a module *)
module Indexing_directive = struct
  type t = Include | Exclude
  let string_of = function Include -> "Include" | Exclude -> "Exclude"
end
```

Apply this when a type has more than one associated operation. The canonical type name inside a module is always `t`. Module name is `UpperCamelCase`.

