## API Design

### Argument order
Optional args first, then positional `dbname`, `coll_name`, resource id, `?timeout` last:
```ocaml
(* Correct signature shape *)
val get :
  ?if_none_match:string ->
  partition_key:string ->
  ?consistency_level:consistency_level ->
  ?timeout:float ->
  string ->   (* dbname *)
  string ->   (* coll_name *)
  string ->   (* doc_id *)
  (int * string, cosmos_error) result IO.t
```

### Return types
```ocaml
(* Data response *)
(int * 'a, cosmos_error) result IO.t

(* No-body response (delete, etc.) *)
(int, cosmos_error) result IO.t

(* With headers (list, query — caller may need continuation token) *)
(int * Response_headers.t * list_result, cosmos_error) result IO.t
```

### Error variants
Add new `cosmos_error` variants at the top of `databases_core.ml` only — never inline:
```ocaml
(* At top of databases_core.ml — extend here *)
type cosmos_error =
  | Timeout_error
  | Connection_error
  | Azure_error of int * Response_headers.t
```

